      "translation": {
        "english_text": "A screen called clever speech for treachery—think about it. Is this human dharma: behaving so outrageously when a woman stands alone and unprotected? You too must have been born among women! Tell me—is this justice? Should you not at least respect my love, which is prepared to sacrifice country, city, mansions, all of it, for a love in accord with conviction? You have studied all the shastras! You have learned all the arts! You have turned the pages of law books! Tell me truthfully—is this dharma? Is this proper?",
        "mode": "prose-faithful",
        "notes": [
          "This immutable utterance spans PDF 12–13 and remains one English unit. `தர்மம்` and `சாஸ்திரம்` retain their source register as `dharma` and `shastras`; the physical page-break word split is not reproduced in English."
        ]
      }
